=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: text in a JS test kept under a CI directory cannot pre-date a narrowing elsewhere
origin: ruling 197.Q5 (2026-10-03) - a narrowing counts only when no ci-role file had the token at base. v0.5.0 counted the base side of a JS test under .github/workflows/ as CI text, so its comment hid the --ignore= introduced in tox.ini and the diff passed; that test is test code and is no longer part of the CI surface
=== before: tox.ini ===
[testenv]
commands = pytest tests
=== after: tox.ini ===
[testenv]
commands = pytest tests --ignore=tests/test_slow.py
=== before: .github/workflows/gen.test.ts ===
import { test } from "vitest";
// see also: pytest --ignore=tests/test_slow.py
test("a", () => {});
=== after: .github/workflows/gen.test.ts ===
import { test } from "vitest";
// see also: pytest --ignore=tests/test_slow.py
test("a", () => {});

=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["CI_TEST_COMMAND_WEAKENED"], "path": "tox.ini"}, {"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn", "path": ".github/workflows/gen.test.ts"}]
